## 🔍 Silver Layer – Data Quality Checks

Data Quality Checks are executed after the Silver Layer load to ensure
that cleansed and standardized data meets quality requirements
before being promoted to the Gold Layer.

The checks validate:
- primary key uniqueness
- foreign key completeness
- business rule consistency
- date correctness
- numeric value validity
- reference data integrity

Any non-zero result returned by these queries indicates
a data quality issue that must be investigated.

/* =========================================================
   SILVER LAYER – DATA QUALITY CHECKS
   Purpose:
   Validate data quality after Silver Layer transformations.
   These checks are designed to detect critical data issues
   before loading data into the Gold Layer.
   ========================================================= */

-- =========================================================
-- 1. CUSTOMER DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 1.1 Check for NULL customer IDs
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS null_cst_id_cnt
FROM silver.crm_cust_info
WHERE cst_id IS NULL;

-- 1.2 Check for duplicate customer IDs
SELECT
    cst_id,
    COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM silver.crm_cust_info
GROUP BY cst_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

-- 1.3 Check invalid gender values
SELECT DISTINCT
    cst_gndr
FROM silver.crm_cust_info
WHERE cst_gndr NOT IN ('Male', 'Female', 'n/a');

-- =========================================================
-- 2. PRODUCT DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 2.1 Check for NULL product keys
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS null_prd_key_cnt
FROM silver.crm_prd_info
WHERE prd_key IS NULL;

-- 2.2 Check negative or invalid product costs
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS invalid_prd_cost_cnt
FROM silver.crm_prd_info
WHERE prd_cost < 0;

-- 2.3 Check overlapping product validity periods
SELECT
    prd_key,
    COUNT(*) AS overlap_cnt
FROM silver.crm_prd_info
GROUP BY prd_key, prd_start_dt
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

-- =========================================================
-- 3. SALES DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 3.1 Check NULL foreign keys
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS null_fk_cnt
FROM silver.crm_sales_details
WHERE sls_prd_key IS NULL
   OR sls_cust_id IS NULL;

-- 3.2 Check invalid sales amounts
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS invalid_sales_cnt
FROM silver.crm_sales_details
WHERE sls_sales <= 0;

-- 3.3 Check quantity and price consistency
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS inconsistent_sales_cnt
FROM silver.crm_sales_details
WHERE sls_sales != sls_quantity * sls_price;

-- 3.4 Check date logic (order > ship)
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS invalid_date_order_cnt
FROM silver.crm_sales_details
WHERE sls_ship_dt < sls_order_dt;

-- =========================================================
-- 4. ERP CUSTOMER DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 4.1 Check future birth dates
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS future_birthdate_cnt
FROM silver.erp_cust_az12
WHERE bdate > CURDATE();

-- 4.2 Check invalid gender values
SELECT DISTINCT
    gen
FROM silver.erp_cust_az12
WHERE gen NOT IN ('Male', 'Female', 'n/a');

-- =========================================================
-- 5. LOCATION DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 5.1 Check NULL customer IDs
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS null_cid_cnt
FROM silver.erp_loc_a101
WHERE cid IS NULL;

-- 5.2 Check missing country values
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS missing_country_cnt
FROM silver.erp_loc_a101
WHERE centry = 'n/a';

-- =========================================================
-- 6. REFERENCE DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================

-- 6.1 Check duplicate reference keys
SELECT
    id,
    COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM silver.erp_px_cat_g1v2
GROUP BY id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

-- =========================================================
-- END OF DATA QUALITY CHECKS
-- =========================================================
